{"id":1145,"date":"2026-06-22T14:46:06","date_gmt":"2026-06-22T12:46:06","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/?p=1145"},"modified":"2026-06-23T08:54:45","modified_gmt":"2026-06-23T06:54:45","slug":"ipmu-2026-report","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/2026\/06\/22\/ipmu-2026-report\/","title":{"rendered":"IPMU 2026 Report"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-black-color\">The <a href=\"https:\/\/www.sbai.uniroma1.it\/conferenze\/ipmu2026\/index.php\">21st International Conference on Information Processing and Management of Uncertainty in Knowledge-Based Systems, IPMU 2026<\/a>, took place in Rome (Italy) on 15-19 June 2026, and it was organised by our friends Barbara Vantaggi and Davide Petturiti (University of la Sapienza). Seven members of our research group attended: Marina Iturrate-Bobes, Nicol\u00e1s Carrizosa, David Nieto-Barba, Dar\u00edo Tagarro, Ignacio Montes, Ra\u00fal P\u00e9rez-Fern\u00e1ndez and Enrique Miranda.<\/mark><\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large is-resized\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" src=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Foto-conjunta-congreso2-1024x768.jpeg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1146\" style=\"width:400px\" srcset=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Foto-conjunta-congreso2-1024x768.jpeg 1024w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Foto-conjunta-congreso2-300x225.jpeg 300w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Foto-conjunta-congreso2-768x576.jpeg 768w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Foto-conjunta-congreso2-1536x1152.jpeg 1536w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Foto-conjunta-congreso2-850x638.jpeg 850w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Foto-conjunta-congreso2.jpeg 1600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-black-color\">The conference program consisted of 14 parallel sessions and four plenary talks. Among the plenary speakers, we had the opportunity to listen to Marco Zaffalon, a frequent collaborator of Enrique Miranda, and \u00c1ngeles Gil, our colleague at the University of Oviedo, who summarised her long career devoted to the analysis of fuzzy data.<\/mark><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-black-color\">The members of IMAGINE organized two special sessions: one on \u201c<em>Aggregation Theory in Non-Traditional Contexts<\/em>\u201d, comprising three presentations, and another on \u201cT<em>heoretical and Applied Aspects of Imprecise Probabilities<\/em>\u201d, comprising nine presentations.<\/mark><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-black-color\">At the conference, we presented seven contributions. On Monday, June 15, during the special session on aggregation theory, Marina Iturrate-Bobes and Ra\u00fal P\u00e9rez-Fern\u00e1ndez presented the papers \u201cTwo-sample goodness-of-fit tests to a location-scale family using OWA-based skewness coefficients\u201d and \u201cAsymptotic confidence intervals for a skewness parameter using OWA functions\u201d.<\/mark><\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\"><div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large is-resized\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"472\" src=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Marina-charla-1024x472.jpeg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1153\" style=\"width:400px\" srcset=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Marina-charla-1024x472.jpeg 1024w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Marina-charla-300x138.jpeg 300w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Marina-charla-768x354.jpeg 768w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Marina-charla-1536x708.jpeg 1536w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Marina-charla-850x392.jpeg 850w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Marina-charla.jpeg 1600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\"><div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large is-resized\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" src=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Raul-charla1-1024x768.jpeg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1147\" style=\"width:400px\" srcset=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Raul-charla1-1024x768.jpeg 1024w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Raul-charla1-300x225.jpeg 300w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Raul-charla1-768x576.jpeg 768w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Raul-charla1-1536x1152.jpeg 1536w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Raul-charla1-850x638.jpeg 850w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Raul-charla1.jpeg 1600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<p><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-black-color\">On Tuesday, June 16, during the special session on imprecise probabilities, Dar\u00edo Tagarro, Nicol\u00e1s Carrizosa, Enrique Miranda and Ignacio Montes presented four papers: \u201cAn order-theoretic study of the credal sets generated by comparative probabilities\u201d, \u201cDecision making with generalized distortion models\u201d, \u201cWeighted Total Variation distances for contextual robustification\u201d, and \u201cOn the commutativity of the aggregation of capacities and the natural extension to gambles\u201d.<\/mark><\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\"><div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" src=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Nico-charla-1024x768.jpeg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1149\" style=\"width:400px\" srcset=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Nico-charla-1024x768.jpeg 1024w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Nico-charla-300x225.jpeg 300w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Nico-charla-768x576.jpeg 768w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Nico-charla-1536x1152.jpeg 1536w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Nico-charla-850x638.jpeg 850w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Nico-charla.jpeg 1600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\"><div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" src=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Dario-charla1-1024x768.jpeg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1150\" style=\"width:400px\" srcset=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Dario-charla1-1024x768.jpeg 1024w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Dario-charla1-300x225.jpeg 300w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Dario-charla1-768x576.jpeg 768w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Dario-charla1-1536x1152.jpeg 1536w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Dario-charla1-850x638.jpeg 850w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Dario-charla1.jpeg 1600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\"><div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" src=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Quique-charla21-1024x768.jpeg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1151\" style=\"width:400px\" srcset=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Quique-charla21-1024x768.jpeg 1024w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Quique-charla21-300x225.jpeg 300w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Quique-charla21-768x576.jpeg 768w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Quique-charla21-1536x1152.jpeg 1536w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Quique-charla21-850x638.jpeg 850w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Quique-charla21.jpeg 1600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\"><div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" src=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Nacho-charl2-1-1024x768.jpeg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1152\" style=\"width:400px\" srcset=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Nacho-charl2-1-1024x768.jpeg 1024w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Nacho-charl2-1-300x225.jpeg 300w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Nacho-charl2-1-768x576.jpeg 768w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Nacho-charl2-1-1536x1152.jpeg 1536w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Nacho-charl2-1-850x638.jpeg 850w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Nacho-charl2-1.jpeg 1600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<p><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-black-color\">Finally, on Wednesday, June 17, David Nieto-Barba presented his paper \u201cOn the specific commutativity with Bayesian conditioning of systematic aggregation rules for probability measures\u201d.<\/mark><\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" src=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/David-charla2-1024x768.jpeg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1154\" style=\"width:400px\" srcset=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/David-charla2-1024x768.jpeg 1024w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/David-charla2-300x225.jpeg 300w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/David-charla2-768x576.jpeg 768w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/David-charla2-1536x1152.jpeg 1536w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/David-charla2-850x638.jpeg 850w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/David-charla2.jpeg 1600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-black-color\">On Thursday, June 18, we enjoyed a guided tour through the city center of Rome, visiting iconic places such as the Trevi Fountain and the Pantheon. Afterwards, we attended a wonderful gala dinner. During the dinner, the traditional awards were given, and Nicol\u00e1s Carrizosa received the IJAR Best Student Paper Award.<\/mark><\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" src=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Nico-premio2.jpeg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1155\" style=\"width:400px\" srcset=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Nico-premio2.jpeg 800w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Nico-premio2-300x225.jpeg 300w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Nico-premio2-768x576.jpeg 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-black-color\">Overall, during these days we enjoyed both the scientific and social aspects of the conference, and we will keep many fond memories of it. Last but not least, we would like to congratulate the organising committee for all the work they put into making this conference such a success. See you in Warsaw at the IPMU 2028 conference!<\/mark><\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" src=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Foto-conjunta-cenagala2-1024x768.jpeg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1156\" style=\"width:400px\" srcset=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Foto-conjunta-cenagala2-1024x768.jpeg 1024w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Foto-conjunta-cenagala2-300x225.jpeg 300w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Foto-conjunta-cenagala2-768x576.jpeg 768w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/up